  "variants_reading": "the per-mm cost is set by the flow's repeater insertion, not by the metal: opening M8/M9 moved the long wire from M6 to M8 (lower RC) and a 60 ps max-transition limit forced denser buffering, and neither moved the register-to-register delay by more than a few percent. A run restricted to M4-M9 failed detailed routing (pin access, DRT-0255) and has no record",
